  "worked_solution": "If $A$ and $B$ are two points on a circle, then the part of the circle which is enclosed between $A$ and $B$ is the *arc $\\overset{⌢}{AB}.$*\n\nTherefore, the correct mathematical statement is the following:\n\n\"*If $A$ and $B$ are two **points** on a circle, then the **arc $\\overset{⌢}{AB}$** is the part of the circle which is enclosed between $A$ and $B.$*\"",
